cant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ITO TAKASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUENAGA MASATO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ITO, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUENAGA, MASATO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A process which is favorable for industrially producing Apelin on a mass scale. This process for producing Apelin or its salt is characterized in that a fused protein or peptide constructed by ligating Apelin optionally having at the N-end a methionine residue, which may be oxidized, to the N-end of a protein or peptide having cysteine at the N-end is subjected to a cleavage reaction of the peptide bond in the amino group side of the cysteine residue. Use of this process makes it possible to industrially produce on a mass scale Apelin which is usable as a remedy, a preventive, etc. for specific diseases.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un procédé permettant de fabriquer industriellement l'apeline à grande échelle. Ce procédé de fabrication de l'apeline et de ses sels est caractérisé en ce qu'une protéine ou un peptide fusionnés construit par ligature de l'apeline possédant éventuellement un résidu de méthionine au niveau de sa terminaison N, et pouvant être oxydé au niveau de la terminaison N d'une protéine ou d'un peptide présentant de la cystéine au niveau de ladite terminaison N, est soumis à une réaction de clivage de la liaison peptidique du groupe latéral amino du résidu de la cystéine. L'invention concerne également le procédé de fabrication industrielle et à grande échelle de l'apeline qui peut être utilisé comme médicament, préventif, etc. contre des maladies spécifiques.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>